  "scope": "Complete schema-based result coordination and saved-fuel materialization move to the product adapter. Native result-domain conversion, successor authority and request assembly, lease fences, journal settlement and winner publication remain with the original owner.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is trusted Leserpent product policy, not the standalone generic VM or an untrusted-input entry. The caller owns bounded image/body admission, reply provenance and original authority. Static consistency does not authenticate receipts or leases.",
    "Callbacks execute once. Earlier native side effects are not rolled back and faults/unwinds are not retried. Raw group results remain subject to the original group coordinator.",
    "The frozen coordinator and materializer share the original evaluator, converters and journals. These comparisons prove coordinator parity, not an independent implementation of those layers.",
    "The private completion matrix deliberately checks four mutating operations without their original operation context; all 20 baseline shape combinations retain LSV2103 refusal. Public reply-entry mutation guards remain unchanged.",
    "Native successor assembly, result conversion/settlement, cancellation/retry coordination, journal ownership, full host-neutral durable recovery, complete vertical compatibility and physical extraction remain open. Native completion and maturity are not promoted.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no Linux, GUI or remote CI run. The existing 280-file standalone checkpoint was integrity-checked, not freshly exported or retested."
  ],
